    "created_at": "2023-06-13T05:24:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-06-13T05:24:47Z",
    "body": "> Yeah, I'm def down with the concept. Question is just if we think there's a necessity for full art-direction (multiple `source` elements) or if it's fine to _just_ provide different-density variants of the same image. I suspect the latter.\r\n\r\nThe `media` attribute was [reintroduced to media element sources](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/6363) yesterday.  Once that is implemented in browsers the video element will support art-directions with multiple `source` elements with media attributes. \r\n\r\nAs a result I think that there's a need for full art-direction of the poster image as well. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
