    "created_at": "2024-03-02T16:39:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-03-02T16:39:29Z",
    "body": "> Yeah, I'm def down with the concept. Question is just if we think there's a necessity for full art-direction (multiple `source` elements) or if it's fine to _just_ provide different-density variants of the same image. I suspect the latter.\r\n\r\nI stumbled into this issue when I looked for how to provide different file type versions of the same poster image – for example JXL + traditional JPEG as fallback. This is possible for `<img>` with the help of `<picture>` and `<source>`. It would be nice to be able to do this for `<video>` poster images as well so that more efficient or better quality images can be used in supporting browsers without making the poster image break in legacy/non-supporting browsers.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
